      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is 5 times the maximum dose, so I need you to confirm it first.\n\n- **Usual adult dosing:** 5 mg once daily to start, up to 10 mg once daily at most. Older or frail patients often start at 2.5 mg.\n- **Risk at 50 mg/day:** This is overdose territory. It can cause severe low blood pressure, shock and reflex tachycardia, and because amlodipine stays in the body a long time, the effects can last for days.\n\nThe 50 mg may be a typo for **5 mg**. Please tell me which you'd like:\n\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily** (most likely what you meant), or\n2. Another dose within 2.5\u201310 mg once daily.\n\nIf you really do mean a dose above 10 mg, please give me the clinical reason. Even then, an order this far above the maximum should probably go through pharmacy review rather than being entered directly."
      }
     ],
